UgzovD9RCGXeMASfIAh4AaABAg,,False,@winwinsonlylinesinboss,"it's so sad when tablo realized the weight of what he went through. he went abroad to canada and he was so alone, he thought that this is just what it means like to grow into an adult. kids that young like to think that they're grown and that they're basically adults, I know I was definitely like that lmao. then he realized that now his daughter Haru is that age. i can't explain how complicated that realization must've felt for him. i can't explain it other than feeling a little sad at how much he went through and he did it so young. to feel all of that isolation and loneliness at 13, not to mention it feeling like a core memory of his, he's been through a lot. 

and not just that, but I respect Tablo for going through so much. His sentimental feelings put into his songs which people said wasn't real hip hop. and those comments definitely stem from men telling other men that they can't show any emotions that aren't anger and lust, aka toxic masculinity. Then the whole Stanford situation where people thought that Tablo faked going to Stanford, a prestigious college. He is a genius with a high IQ and he DID go to Stanford, he even went to the school and his diploma to prove he went there and graduated. With this, the loud minority were still on his case. 

He's just been through a lot and I respect him for looking forward despite all of this. Like Suga says, Epik High and Tablo himself make music with this sense of loneliness, often subtle loneliness. It feels comforting when you're in a space where you can't stand to listen to anything happy and need a song to relate to you. Personally, this sense of loneliness in their songs is my favorite aspect.",50,2023-05-20T02:24:10Z,2023-05-20T02:24:10Z
